WEBVTT

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.260
German Democratic Republic 
Wittstock Training Grounds

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.330
Lieutenant Pham Thi Lan died in battle,

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.000
trying to stop Hohenstein.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:24.960
Hohenstein killed her.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:26.730
No...

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.050
You bastard!

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.060
Why?

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:43.100
Why didn't you kill her?!

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:48.190
She's with the Stasi! She's our enemy!

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:52.190
What, you couldn't kill her because 
she's your sister? Your lover?!

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.820
You traitor!

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:07.420
So we failed to recapture Captain Bernhard?

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:08.630
Yes.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:11.170
But this primed the pump.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.920
Two brigades from Schwerin have risen up.

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:19.160
Three battalions from Leipzig have 
also responded to our call.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:25.990
Ground forces are to continue 
their advance on East Berlin.

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:26.690
Yes, sir.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:36.340
I understand that you were uncertain, but...

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.480
Yeah, I know.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.930
It's all my fault.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:49.920
I'll kill Lise with my own hands.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:54.960
Theodor...

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:34.190
German Democratic Republic 
Bebersee Base

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:39.190
So Heim has taken action?

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:42.090
He hit us while we were on the front lines.

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.630
I'm sorry.

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:44.950
It's not your fault.

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:47.450
Axmann must have sided with him.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:50.670
He's the tricky sort.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:55.960
But we should think about what 
to do with Lieutenant Hohenstein.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.460
She can be relied upon to fight.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.970
She has nothing left, after all.

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:06.470
A sad story.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:09.140
Very well. I'll leave it to you.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:13.230
Now I must discuss with the others 
how to deal with the rebels.

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:17.250
Then Werewolf Battalion 
will return to the front

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:19.330
and continue battle with the BETAs.

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:22.950
I'll leave the Borkwalde Squadron 
here to deal with the rebels.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:25.990
We are the party's sword and shield.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.750
We will win the day.

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:29.410
Indeed.

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:35.800
She is talented.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:41.450
That's probably why she refuses 
to remain a dog forever.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:05:01.240
Parts of the NPA rebelled against 
the Stasi government this morning.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.660
It's a de facto civil war.

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:09.530
<i>The Stasi shows no regard for the people's safety.</i>

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:12.710
<i>To preserve their own power, 
they were even willing</i>

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:17.140
<i>to purge Alfred Strachwitz, 
the man who saved East Germany.</i>

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:19.770
<i>That is the Stasi's true nature.</i>

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.550
Who is this?

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:25.380
Major General Franz Heim, leader of the rebels.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:28.010
He was known as a dove.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:34.560
<i>This is the time to rise against the 
Stasi and save our country.</i>

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.940
<i>For the rebuilding of East Germany to take—</i>

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:42.940
The West German government is presently 
discussing their response to the rebellion.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:47.950
Do we support the present government, 
to bolster the lines against the BETA,

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:51.990
or overthrow the government and unify Germany?

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:54.950
The majority of the government 
wants the former.

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:59.460
Why are you telling me this?

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:04.340
The 666th TSF Squadron is aiding the rebellion.

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:10.090
You want me to contact them in East Germany,

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:13.400
and get something that'll help us 
persuade the government?

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:14.970
That's it, isn't it?

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:20.590
Understood.

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:23.950
Second Lieutenant Kirke Steinhoff 
will carry out the mission.

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:26.240
This mission is dangerous and unofficial.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:28.740
I owe them.

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:33.700
No matter what happens, 
I'll wipe your ass for you.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:37.000
I can wipe my own ass.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:45.590
It's a nice ass.

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:50.760
German Democratic Republic 
Seelow Heights

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:56.370
BETA echelon has reached 
the third defensive line.

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:57.890
At this rate, they'll break through.

00:06:58.190 --> 00:06:59.390
Where are the TSFs?

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:02.150
No good. We have no units capable of fighting.

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:07.650
Sorry for making you wait.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:11.160
The Werewolf Battalion will 
return to the battlefield.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:14.460
It's hunting time.

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:16.120
All units, follow me!

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:17.200
Roger!

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:18.990
Damn it.

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:21.620
Just a bit ago, they left the 
battlefield without permission!

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:24.920
The way they're using their units is strange.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:29.400
German Democratic Republic 
Neuruppin

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:27.250
What's happening at the rear?

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:41.190
The Werewolf Battalion has returned to 
the Oder-Neisse absolute defense line.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:45.480
They shouldn't be able to 
interfere with us for a while.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:47.220
What's the situation in Berlin?

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:50.440
We've sighted a Stasi tank unit 
on the Havel River's west side.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:54.450
They intend to intercept the revolutionary 
army before it can enter the capital?

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:58.990
All the units across the country that have 
risen up with us are coming to join us.

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:02.220
In a ground fight, we should be 
more than a match for them.

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:04.170
What's the situation with Axmann?

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:07.960
He says he's temporarily acting alone 
to execute the plan we discussed.

00:08:08.510 --> 00:08:12.470
General, the TSF units from Leipzig have arrived.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:17.990
The 612th TSF Squadron's 
Second Lieutenant Löwith,

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:20.480
Second Lieutenant Meissen, 
and Lieutenant Artner.

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:22.980
You're the Schwarzesmarken pilots, right?

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:28.320
We were able to survive because you 
defeated the Heavy Laser-classes.

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:32.610
We'll follow your orders. Use us as you see fit.

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:35.570
Right. That's a big help.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:38.690
Trouble, General!

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:46.830
<i>At a time when the nation must unite to overcome 
grave danger, Western Theatre Forces...</i>

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:51.880
<i>No, the rebellion has advanced on East Berlin.</i>

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:57.170
<i>The rebellion attacked a front-line 
base, killing multiple personnel</i>

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:58.890
<i>and stealing the TSFs stationed there.</i>

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:00.430
<i>During the battle,</i>

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:06.650
<i>Irisdina Bernhard, Commander of the 
666th, was fatally struck by a bullet.</i>

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:08.650
It's a bluff.

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:11.020
He's trying to make us panic.

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:13.380
<i>They care only for power and are willing</i>

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:17.530
<i>to use force to achieve their ambitions. 
They are traitors to the country.</i>

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:22.290
<i>No, they are the enemy of all humanity, 
endangering the entire world!</i>

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:24.660
You're the one who's humanity's enemy!

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:32.140
<i>We have requested aid from the West 
German government and the UN,</i>

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:36.260
<i>and we will work with these militaries 
to put down the rebellion—</i>

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:38.950
Damn that Schmidt.

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:40.930
He works fast.

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:45.270
But will the West agree to the Stasi's request?

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:47.190
About that...

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:52.570
The West German government sent a special 
messenger to the revolutionary army.

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:56.070
Her name is Second Lieutenant Kirke Steinhoff.

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:04.700
West Germany is uncertain which of us to support.

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:10.080
And they want the Second Lieutenant to 
find something to help them decide...

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:14.120
But the Stasi have learned of this.

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:18.430
TSFs and bombers are gathering at 
Herzberg Base, to the south.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:22.720
They're willing to take us out along 
with the messenger if they have to.

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:25.890
Comrade Lieutenant, at this rate...

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:30.070
If we can just neutralize the TSFs,

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:32.650
we can use our air force to handle them.

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:36.260
We can set a trap.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:39.970
Leak the location of the meeting 
with the messenger,

00:10:39.970 --> 00:10:41.770
and they'll go for it.

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.300
Then, we'll wipe them out.

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:48.620
If we can't get more allies, 
we'll decrease the number of enemies.

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:56.190
German Democratic Republic 
Inside East Berlin

00:10:59.140 --> 00:11:00.680
The Berlin Wall.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:03.130
It's clean, unlike the West side.

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:05.680
Wonder what would happen 
if you put graffiti on it...

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:08.680
Two Germanys, huh?

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:10.550
It's a relic of the Cold War.

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:14.820
Some of my relatives have families 
that are divided by this wall.

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:17.820
There's the checkpoint.

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:19.370
Don't screw this up.

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:28.850
West German Military, 101st Infantry.

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:33.080
Lieutenant Stefan Müller and Second 
Lieutenant Annelotte Rottenmeier.

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:36.500
We're bringing aid for the people of East Berlin.

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:39.080
We have a pass from the UN.

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:43.050
Annelotte Rottenmeier...

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:48.100
Get out.

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:49.660
You're under arrest.

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:51.760
Hey, wait!

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:53.830
We have official UN orders!

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:05.080
Kirke Steinhoff, correct?

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.330
I'm Suzy Dzap, of Grosser Bär.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:12.180
Bebersee Base

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:13.170
Attention, all units!

00:12:13.590 --> 00:12:16.440
We've learned that Heim is meeting

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:19.670
his collaborators at the 
Albert Hotel in Neuruppin.

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:24.580
Our squadron will attack this hotel 
and secure Major General Heim.

00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:25.930
Dead or alive.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:28.040
Is this a trap?

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:29.770
It seems too easy.

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:32.380
We've confirmed that Heim is on the move.

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:36.560
And it's unlikely the rebellion would endanger 
their messenger from the West.

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:37.430
But—

00:12:37.430 --> 00:12:38.770
Come to think of it,

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:42.570
your brother is participating 
in the rebellion, isn't he?

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:47.370
Your opinion is worthless.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:49.150
We're done here.

00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:51.460
Borkwalde Squadron, heading out!

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:03.630
Outskirts of Neuruppin

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:07.220
I can see it.

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:10.890
The target, the Albert Hotel.

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:13.970
Split up and monitor the surrounding area!

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:42.220
Something is wrong...

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:50.340
Wh-What?

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:55.930
Chaff! Data links down!

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.400
What is this?!

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:06.420
Wh-Where did it come from?

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:11.690
Attack from the surrounding buildings!

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:16.050
Split up!

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:17.940
Hit the TSFs in their blind spots!

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:19.050
Roger!

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:28.850
Hurry!

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:41.480
I told you so...

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:45.700
Squadron Commander, unknowns are 
approaching from the south!

00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:47.970
This is...

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:55.540
I knew it.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:04.290
Brother!

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:08.550
You used us as a decoy?

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:11.550
We had no choice.

00:15:11.780 --> 00:15:14.900
But how can you use a city as a battlefield?!

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:22.570
My comrades in the 666th Squadron fought

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:26.270
for the cause of defending the people.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:29.530
Where is the cause in this battle?

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:34.280
This plan was their idea.

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:39.830
We'll knock them out now, before they regroup!

00:15:40.070 --> 00:15:40.960
Roger!

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:47.000
Don't mess with me, rebels!

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:57.720
Don't get in my way, Brother!

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:03.400
You are my enemy!

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:05.210
All right...

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:08.820
Then I'll use force

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:12.740
to make you understand!

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:18.240
A battle in Neuruppin?

00:16:18.570 --> 00:16:19.450
Yes.

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:22.750
TSF squads are fighting each other right now.

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:33.470
Second Lieutenant Meitzen!

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:35.470
Damn you!

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.100
Damn it! My left jump unit!

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:48.600
Are you okay, Anett?

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:49.940
Comrade Lieutenant!

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:51.880
Don't get crazy with your sword.

00:16:51.880 --> 00:16:53.900
They're more mobile than we are.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:59.260
But if we work together, no one can beat us.

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:00.140
Let's go!

00:17:00.140 --> 00:17:01.040
Right!

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:04.590
She called me "Anett"...

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:19.390
It's useless to resist, Brother.

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:22.280
No one can disobey the Stasi.

00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:25.110
I've learned that in these past three years!

00:17:27.030 --> 00:17:28.400
Dreams...

00:17:31.220 --> 00:17:32.650
Hopes...

00:17:33.930 --> 00:17:37.280
Just give up on them already!

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:02.560
N-No...

00:18:03.860 --> 00:18:05.820
What are you doing, Hohenstein?!

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:08.690
H-Hurry and back me up!

00:18:09.220 --> 00:18:11.300
What's wrong, Lieutenant Hohenste—

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:41.760
Just wait, Brother.

00:18:43.650 --> 00:18:45.270
I will

00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:48.020
wake you up!

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:10.580
Lise!

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:49.010
Brother...

00:20:56.900 --> 00:21:01.860
You still think you can win?

00:21:03.170 --> 00:21:07.220
The rebellion is just a bunch of idiots...

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:10.440
And liars.

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:15.500
They'll soon flee...

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:17.910
That's why

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:24.350
I tried to save you...

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:29.510
You're so stupid and stubborn...

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:32.370
Why?

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:33.830
Tell me.

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:36.020
I don't understand!

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:40.230
Why do you like the rebellion so much?

00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:43.400
They're just using you!

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:46.210
They say they'll change East Germany,

00:21:46.210 --> 00:21:47.210
but that's a lie.

00:21:47.210 --> 00:21:48.410
It's not possible!

00:21:48.670 --> 00:21:51.590
There's no way it's possible!

00:21:58.410 --> 00:22:03.150
People can't trust other people.

00:22:04.410 --> 00:22:06.770
If you trust someone,

00:22:07.570 --> 00:22:11.930
that means they might kill you.

00:22:20.220 --> 00:22:24.790
Hey... Come with me, Brother.

00:22:25.790 --> 00:22:30.950
I just want to be with you...

00:22:34.530 --> 00:22:37.210
I can't go with you.

00:22:38.530 --> 00:22:39.520
I have

00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:43.510
a wish I must make come true.

00:22:47.320 --> 00:22:49.340
I'm sorry, Lise.

00:22:50.740 --> 00:22:52.600
Dad told me to,

00:22:53.210 --> 00:22:55.350
but I couldn't protect you.

00:22:55.970 --> 00:22:59.790
You saved me from the Stasi.

00:23:06.980 --> 00:23:07.860
That's why

00:23:08.710 --> 00:23:11.750
I have to save you now.

00:23:14.680 --> 00:23:17.870
Because I'm...

00:23:19.480 --> 00:23:20.790
I'm your...

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:24.020
I'm your brother.

00:23:28.990 --> 00:23:31.930
Brother...
